{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>A persistent plague.</b> Like סלון (a thorn), ממאיר; and since סלון is like קוץ (thorn), ממאיר is like מכאיב (causing pain). The second mem in the word ממארת is a root letter; it is not derived from מארה. The reason he did not mention silk and [goat-]hair [is that] perhaps Scripture speaks of what is commonly found, as in the sense of 'When you see your enemy's donkey' (Exodus 23:5), and likewise the law of the horse and the mule. Or it is possible that the plague occurs only in wool and linen."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:57.309745855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}